{"type":"record","name":"LiquidityWallTargets","namespace":"com.optionsedge.contracts.liquiditywall","doc":"liq-AA liquidity targets (es-liquidity-wall-service): the nearest sizeable resting blocks above and below the spot, once per closed bucket, on the compacted topic futures.liquidity-wall.targets under the single key CME|<contract>. A DISPLAY of where size rests, chosen from one Friday; not a finding and no claim that price travels to a block. Every ratio is an integer in thousandths; every closed vocabulary is a string. VERSION 2 (id 3413, liq-AA clean cells): each target gains cellKey, cellPrimary, cellCount and resolved, decided by the service so that the page draws only what is flagged. Version 1 is id 3411 and stays registered and readable.","fields":[{"name":"schemaVersion","type":"int","doc":"1","default":1},{"name":"depthEnvironment","type":"string","doc":"environment literal of the admitted depth frames"},{"name":"contract","type":"string","doc":"the contract table's row"},{"name":"configFingerprint","type":"string","doc":"the wall engine's configuration fingerprint"},{"name":"bucketEnd","type":"long","doc":"bucket end, epoch ms"},{"name":"quality","type":"string","doc":"the bucket's quality"},{"name":"state","type":"string","doc":"READY, WARMING_UP, OUT_OF_SESSION, NO_SPOT, NO_BOOK or CALENDAR_UNKNOWN"},{"name":"sessionDate","type":["null","string"],"doc":"trade date of the tracking session (the SPX cash close that ends it), null out of session","default":null},{"name":"spotTick","type":["null","long"],"doc":"the spot print's tick","default":null},{"name":"thresholdThousandths","type":"int","doc":"display multiple of the typical size a block must reach (3000 = 3.0x); a DISPLAY setting, not a finding"},{"name":"maxPerSide","type":"int","doc":"largest number of targets shown per side"},{"name":"reachTicksWanted","type":"int","doc":"how far from the spot the search goes (200 = 50 points)"},{"name":"typicalAbove","type":["null","long"],"doc":"median size per occupied price on the ask side over the trailing hour of samples, null while warming up","default":null},{"name":"typicalBelow","type":["null","long"],"doc":"same for the bid side","default":null},{"name":"reachAboveTicks","type":["null","long"],"doc":"how far above the spot the book actually extends, at most reachTicksWanted","default":null},{"name":"reachBelowTicks","type":["null","long"],"doc":"how far below the spot the book actually extends, at most reachTicksWanted","default":null},{"name":"nearContractsAbove","type":["null","long"],"doc":"contracts over the nearest nearPrices occupied ask prices above the spot","default":null},{"name":"nearContractsBelow","type":["null","long"],"doc":"contracts over the nearest nearPrices occupied bid prices below the spot","default":null},{"name":"nearPrices","type":"int","doc":"8","default":8},{"name":"targets","type":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"record","name":"LiquidityWallTarget","namespace":"com.optionsedge.contracts.liquiditywall","doc":"one displayed liquidity target: a sizeable resting block above or below the spot. A display object, not a finding.","fields":[{"name":"targetId","type":"string","doc":"side|tick|firstShownBucketEnd, unique within a trade date"},{"name":"side","type":"string","doc":"ABOVE (an ask block above the spot) or BELOW (a bid block below the spot)"},{"name":"tick","type":"long","doc":"ES quarter-point tick of the block's price (price = tick / 4)"},{"name":"distanceTicks","type":"long","doc":"ticks from the spot print at this bucket to the block (positive both sides)"},{"name":"size","type":"long","doc":"contracts resting at that single price at this bucket's close"},{"name":"multipleThousandths","type":"long","doc":"size over the trailing-hour typical per-price size of its side, in thousandths"},{"name":"firstShownBucketEnd","type":"long","doc":"bucket end at which the block was first shown (t0 of its record)"},{"name":"status","type":"string","doc":"WAITING, REACHED, PASSED, CONSUMED or PULLED, from the in-service tracker"},{"name":"reachedAfterMs","type":["null","long"],"doc":"ms from t0 to the first print within the tolerance, null while waiting","default":null},{"name":"pastTicks","type":"long","doc":"furthest ticks past the block so far (0 before it is reached)"},{"name":"resolvedAtBucketEnd","type":["null","long"],"doc":"bucket end at which the block was found consumed or pulled, null otherwise","default":null},{"name":"live","type":"boolean","doc":"true when the block still qualifies at this bucket, false for a resolved one kept on view for a short time"},{"name":"wallClusterId","type":["null","string"],"default":null,"doc":"clusterId of the live wall (Layer B) whose ticks contain this block on the same side, null when no wall shows it; the page draws ONE bar for the block and adds the multiple and the chip to the wall bar"},{"name":"touches","type":"int","default":0,"doc":"role-flip tracker: touches counted so far (a touch = a print within the tolerance of the block's price from its original side, after price was at least the reset distance away)"},{"name":"flipState","type":"string","default":"TESTING","doc":"role-flip tracker: TESTING, INVADED, RETEST_HELD, RETEST_FAILED, RETEST_UNRESOLVED or NO_RETEST. The page draws the tilted line, the colour and the chip ONLY from INVADED onward"},{"name":"flipKind","type":["null","string"],"default":null,"doc":"R_TO_S (a resistance block invaded upward, now acting below price) or S_TO_R (a support block invaded downward), set at INVADED"},{"name":"invadedAtMs","type":["null","long"],"default":null,"doc":"bucket end at which the invasion was recorded"},{"name":"sizeHistory","type":{"type":"array","items":["null","long"]},"default":[],"doc":"the block's price's resting size at -30, -25, -20, -15, -10, -5 and 0 minutes (seven entries, oldest first, the last is the size now); an entry is null when the book was not read at that time or the price was outside the search distance then. Aligned to the five-minute marks of data time. Empty before the first mark."},{"name":"highestSize","type":["null","long"],"default":null,"doc":"the largest size seen at that price over the history and since the block was first shown"},{"name":"highestAtMs","type":["null","long"],"default":null,"doc":"bucket end (or five-minute mark) of that largest size"},{"name":"eatenContracts","type":"long","default":0,"doc":"since first shown: contracts the size lost between buckets that were matched by contracts printed at the price"},{"name":"pulledContracts","type":"long","default":0,"doc":"since first shown: contracts the size lost without prints at the price"},{"name":"addedContracts","type":"long","default":0,"doc":"since first shown: contracts the size gained between buckets"},{"name":"eatenTape","type":{"type":"array","items":["null","long"]},"default":[],"doc":"contracts EATEN by trades in the five minutes ending at each of the seven marks of sizeHistory (the last = since the latest mark); null before the block was tracked. Eaten = executions at the block's price against the block, capped at the size lost in that bucket; see the requirement LT-R-14"},{"name":"pulledTape","type":{"type":"array","items":["null","long"]},"default":[],"doc":"contracts PULLED (lost without executions, after moves are taken out) in the same windows"},{"name":"movedTape","type":{"type":"array","items":["null","long"]},"default":[],"doc":"contracts that left the block and reappeared within 2 ticks on the same side in the same bucket (a move, not a pull) in the same windows"},{"name":"movedContracts","type":"long","default":0,"doc":"since first shown: the moved total"},{"name":"pullTiming","type":["null","string"],"default":null,"doc":"when the pulling began, from the first bucket at which the pulled total reached a tenth of the block's first size: AFTER_TOUCH (the block had been touched), NEAR (price within 12 ticks) or FAR; null until it begins"},{"name":"firstPullAtMs","type":["null","long"],"default":null,"doc":"bucket end of that first bucket"},{"name":"growing","type":"boolean","default":false,"doc":"true while this block's size, read every bucket as the median of its last five closing sizes (the wall engine's own smoothing length), has risen at least once since the block first appeared and has never fallen: any rise starts it (100, 102, 105), an unchanged reading keeps it, and the first lower reading (even slightly) ends it for the rest of this block's life (it does not blink again if it later rises). Judged per block independently; a block that disappears and reappears is a new block. Computed in the service from the owner's words (a bar going consistently up); no multiple, no minimum count of readings; the page only draws it (a soft blink)"},{"name":"growthRatioThousandths","type":["null","long"],"default":null,"doc":"information only, never a gate: the current reading over the size the block first had, in thousandths; null when not growing"},{"name":"speedMilliLnPerMinute","type":["null","long"],"default":null,"doc":"growing blocks only: the relative growth rate, the natural logarithm of (current reading over the size the block first had) divided by the minutes since it was first seen, times 1000, truncated; computed in the service. Null when the block is not growing or has been watched less than one minute"},{"name":"speedRank","type":["null","int"],"default":null,"doc":"rank among the growing blocks by that speed (1 = fastest), ties to the block nearest the spot; null when not ranked"},{"name":"growingCount","type":"int","default":0,"doc":"how many blocks are growing at this bucket (both sides together)"},{"name":"blinking","type":"boolean","default":false,"doc":"true for ONE block at most in the whole record: the fastest growing block (speedRank 1). The page blinks only the block with this flag"},{"name":"changeThousandths","type":["null","long"],"default":null,"doc":"the popover's change chip: the size now over the size at the window start minus one, in thousandths, computed in the service"},{"name":"changeWindowMinutes","type":["null","int"],"default":null,"doc":"the window of that change: 30 when the 30-minute reading exists, else the longest reading available (5 to 25)"},{"name":"cellKey","type":"long","default":0,"doc":"the futures 5-point cell of the block's price: floor(tick / 20). Blocks with the same key are grouped by the service; the page places the primary of each group at its own SPX cell"},{"name":"cellPrimary","type":"boolean","default":true,"doc":"true for the ONE block of its cell group that the page draws as a bar: the live block with the largest current size (ties to the nearer to the spot); resolved blocks are never primary"},{"name":"cellCount","type":"int","default":1,"doc":"how many live (not resolved) blocks the cell group holds; the page shows a small count chip when it is above 1"},{"name":"resolved","type":"boolean","default":false,"doc":"true when the block is consumed or pulled (size 0 or fate found) and kept on view only as a dim tick; never drawn as a bar"}]}},"default":[],"doc":"the targets, above then below, nearest first within a side"},{"name":"bookState","type":"string","default":"LIVE","doc":"the words for the page: LIVE when the closed bucket's book was read (quality LIVE), else the bucket's quality (DEGRADED, RESTART, STALE, GAP) so the page can say why the targets are carried"},{"name":"lastLiveBucketEnd","type":["null","long"],"default":null,"doc":"bucket end of the last bucket whose book was read (quality LIVE), null before the first"},{"name":"carriedBuckets","type":"int","default":0,"doc":"how many successive buckets the target list has been carried without a readable book (0 when live)"},{"name":"label","type":"string","doc":"the constant DISPLAY_NOT_A_FINDING","default":"DISPLAY_NOT_A_FINDING"}]}